Z||000000||dodger||01-25-2000||01:03 AM||||Anyone know of an emergency kit that fits nicely somewhere in the SE. You know, cables, flares etc.||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||01-25-2000||01:38 AM||||I don't know of any kit but I got a canvas bag and put all that kind of stuff into it myself. It fits nicely in the spare tire area.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||01-25-2000||07:14 AM||||I also use a sports bag and keep it in the spare tire well.  If you turn the spare tire up-side-down it will give you a nice hole to store stuff.<BR>I keep a qt of oil, a gallon of anti-freeze, jumper cables, assortment of tools, towel, work gloves, hand cleaner, etc. up front.  I also carry a booster battery (gel acid battery with short jumper cables attached) in the trunk.  It has bailed me out when my alternator died on the way to the airport on occaision.  When I got back in town I connected the booster battery to the car battery via jumper cables with the booster in the trunk and drove home with no problems.<P>One time as I got out of the car at the airport I accidently hit the reading light switch with my briefcase and turned it on.  When I got back a week later the battery was dead.  I jumped it of with the booster battery.<BR>This has been a great $40 investment.  I got it at Sam's.  It has 855CCA.  The new ones have 1000CCA.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||01-25-2000||01:56 PM||||The battery booster sound very interesting! Who makes it?||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||01-25-2000||01:59 PM||||There are a number of people carrying those. K-mart, Wallmart, pepboys, autozone, etc, all have them.||||reg||1
