Z||000018||Monkeyman||01-26-2000||04:41 AM||||I hate to ruin a couple of our reputations here, but I must defend myself (and dogtired).  Neither of us take illegal drugs.  Both of us however take various prescription drugs (very legal and safe) for chronic medical conditions.  I'm diabetic with slightly high blood pressure.  I'll leave dog to explain his medical problems if he cares to.  I neither take nor do I condone the use of illegal substances in any form at any time!!  I was into the drug scene when I was much younger and much stupider.  I have, however, grown up since then.  I think this was started as a joke a long time ago.  Like I said, I hate to ruin my "reputation", but I thought that I needed to clear this up.  <B>I DO NOT TAKE ILLEGAL DRUGS NOR DO I CONDONE THE USE OF THEM!!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Phil||01-26-2000||08:11 AM||||If you will notice I never accused anyone but all this casual referance to taking drugs is read by many people and gives the impression that it is the right and proper thing to do. Monkey(just using you as an example) do you want your son to read this forum and keep seeing his daddy talking about needing his medication with the conotation that it's not for medicinal purposes? Kids minds are strange "My daddy thinks it's alright to use them so they can't be that bad" Scary thought isn't it? <BR>Tell somebody a lie long enough and it becomes the truth.||||reg||1
Z||000020||stsmithgt||01-26-2000||02:31 PM||||Beer? Wine? Cigarettes?  Yes, they are all drugs. Just because there legall doesn't make them any better. I was perscribed DURACT not too long ago.  I later got a call from the pharmasist to find out if I was still alive.  Nice huh?  Duract can kill more than just a back pain.  I found plenty of info on the web about it after the fact. OH I've got to go my beer is getting warm next to my cigarette. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">(kidding)||||reg||1
Z||000021||Monkeyman||01-26-2000||07:30 PM||||I don't drink much (just an occasional beer-BTW, Lowenbrau is my favorite in case I'm ever over at someones house), but I do smoke like a chimney.  Nothing is good if it's taken to excess (well...almost nothing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<BR>Phil-I can see your point about the medication thing.  My son thinks it's funny, but I realize that not everyone's kids would understand.  As of this point I will do my best to refrain from mentioning my alleged medicine habit.  If I forget, just let me know.  I won't be offended.  And I don't mind being used for an example.  My parole officer does it all the time. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 01-26-2000).]||||reg||1
